# SimpleOS fabricated-`rt_*` ELF ACCOUNTING -- read by
# scripts/check/check-simpleos-fabricated-rt-elf.shs
#
# Format: `<entry-key> <symbol> <justification...>`; `#` starts a comment.
# `<entry-key>` is the kernel ELF's basename without `.elf`. `*` applies to
# every entry. A row with NO justification text is REJECTED by the gate --
# accounting without a reason is just an allowlist, and an allowlist is what
# let `rt_index_of` ship.
#
# WHAT A ROW MEANS
#   "This symbol's body in the LINKED kernel is a constant return, and nil/0 is
#    the CORRECT answer at every call site, for the reason written here."
#
# WHAT A ROW IS NOT
#   It is not a place to silence a new failure. The gate enumerates from the
#   ELF, so a symbol you have never seen before is a NEW fabrication: implement
#   it in the arch's boot/baremetal_stubs.c. Adding a row instead is how the
#   45-CSS-property data loss happened.
#
# THE INCIDENT THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE OF (2026-08-09)
#   `("index_of", 1)` joined cranelift's `is_bare_builtin_collection_method`
#   allowlist on 2026-08-01, routing `.index_of()` to `rt_index_of`. No arch
#   stub file defined it, so boot/auto_stubs.c's ~4,023 weak zero-returning
#   definitions FABRICATED a body -- `xor %eax,%eax; ret`. `index_of` answered
#   0 instead of 11; every caller reads 0 as "not found"; all 45 `:root` CSS
#   custom properties vanished in the guest. Fixed at 1f1c00aa578.
#   `rt_index_of` is DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this file: it is a text/collection
#   primitive, nil is never the right answer, and the fix is a real body.
#   Any kernel ELF still carrying a constant-return `rt_index_of` predates that
#   fix and MUST fail this gate.
#
# ARCH ASYMMETRY, RECORDED
#   Only x86_64 links `boot/auto_stubs.c`; aarch64 and riscv fail closed at the
#   link because nothing fabricates for them. That asymmetry is deliberate and
#   is the reason every row below is x86_64. It is not a licence: this gate
#   reads the ELF, so it polices any arch's kernel that grows a constant-return
#   body, fabricated or hand-written.
#
# Measured 2026-08-09 on build/simpleos_wm_fullscreen_evidence/
# simpleos_wm_production_desktop.elf: 417 `rt_*` symbols, 95 with a
# constant-return body (50 weak from auto_stubs.c, 45 strong hand-written
# `return NIL_VALUE;` bodies in arch/x86_64/boot/rt_extras.c and
# baremetal_stubs.c). 94 are accounted below; the 95th is `rt_index_of`.

simpleos_wm_production_desktop rt_arm_virtio_blk_queue_base ARM virtio-blk MMIO seam; not wired on the x86_64 boot path, the driver is selected by arch
